fact WorkItem(id: "WI-082", description: some(value: "Kernel extension: allow Quoted to reference an external source file. Either as a new field form (e.g. Quoted with file path argument) or via a separate construct. Driven by lf1 example, where the Mavic2Pro inner stabilization loop is roughly 100 lines of vendor C++ that should ride along verbatim alongside the anthill spec; inlining as an escaped string literal is impractical. Proposal needed: kernel-spec section 4.2 Quoted Terms, syntax plus scoping rules plus how the referenced path resolves relative to the spec file."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-04-27T09:36:51Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-082", author: "user", content: "Closed: design changed. Inner-loop C++ (mavic_base.{cpp,hpp}) is carried as hand-authored sibling files in cpp/, copied into the generated project tree by the build script. No kernel extension to Quoted needed for lf1; if a future use case requires inline external-file references, reopen with a fresh design.", at: "2026-04-27T09:36:43Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-082", author: "user", content: "Phase A step (b) (define HandlerAction carrier) extracted to standalone WI-389, which intentionally does NOT depend on WI-075 — the Pure/Throw subset Error needs has no snapshot/push_choice requirement. WI-082 retains its WI-075 dependency only for the Choice/Suspend/Branch portion (steps c, e). Also: step (f) attributes the default Error handler to 'WI-070's scope' — that is a typo; the Error ticket is WI-073 (WI-070 is the Modify follow-up). Error is now tracked as WI-389 (carrier) -> WI-073 (Error Throw handler) -> WI-195 (bundle wiring).", at: "2026-06-05T05:28:26Z")
